C\n- Source repository: `/root/projects/tiered-serve`\n- Source HEAD: `5d56a972bb80444671b9d27293e3fa18076c0d58`\n- Consolidated patch SHA-256: `95ad90192897b34d11f79f0cbc541552a61346cacd60d99b01bfdeb2fecf0c92`\n- Files changed: 27\n\n## Startup order\n\n1. `serving_max_batched_tokens.patch` (or its `from_1024` variant)\n2. `serving_performance_suite.patch`\n3. `apply_cd3.sh /root/projects/tiered-serve`\n\n`apply_cd3.sh` verifies and applies the consolidated `cd3_current.patch`.\nIt is idempotent. The old two-stage patch files are retained only as rollback\nartifacts and are not loaded at container startup.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis snapshot contains the current CD3 weight, fused-GEMM, KV codec, CPU\nweight/KV encoders, benchmark, serving integration, model configuration, and\nCD3 tests. Weight encode defaults to CPU; CUDA is used only to stage completed\ncompressed buffers and for decode/fused-MM. The legacy GPU encoder is available\nonly through the explicit debug override `TIERED_SERVE_CD3_WEIGHT_CPU_ENCODE=0`.\nUnrelated working-tree changes were intentionally excluded.\n\nThe CPU KV encoder additionally contains the 2026-09-01 optimization set:\n\n- block-owner, single-source-pass encoding;\n- min/max exception-free fast path;\n- SVE2 predicate counting on the exception path;\n- NEON hierarchical packing of 16 three-bit codes;\n- uninitialized temporary exception scratch.\n\nDirect-to-persistent Packed20 packing was measured but not retained because it\nwas 3–6% slower for medium and large batches.\n\nThe consolidated snapshot additionally contains:\n\n- host-native CD3 weight encoding with 64-row stripe parallelism;\n- adaptive OpenMP team sizing for a single KV compression worker;\n- batched NumPy KV slot allocation instead of a per-block Python loop;\n- production fused-MM crossover calibration through N=128 on GH200.\n- 128-thread standalone CD3 decode, with two logical chunks per thread;\n- two half-width live output accumulators with the same two 128-bit stores